<Bindings>
	<!--
		Daseeki Bags 2.0 keybindings (audit §10.2).

		LOAD CONTRACT: this file is auto-discovered by the client because it sits at
		the addon root and is named Bindings.xml. It must NOT be listed as a file
		entry in Daseeki-Bags2.toc / v2.toc. Doing so ALSO feeds it to the generic
		UI-XML parser, which has no Binding element and emits a LUA_WARNING per
		binding on every load. See the matching note in the .toc files.

		Action names are DASEEKIBAGS2_* so they never collide with the live 1.x
		DASEEKIBAGS_* bindings while both addons are installed, and so any key the
		owner has already bound survives untouched.

		Labels come from the BINDING_HEADER_DASEEKIBAGS2 / BINDING_CATEGORY_DASEEKIBAGS2
		/ BINDING_NAME_DASEEKIBAGS2_* globals set in core.lua. header= sits on the
		first binding only: it opens the group and the following bindings fall under
		it (the shipped Era idiom, cf. AtlasLootClassic and GatherMate2).

		Each body is guarded so a keypress before the handler exists is a harmless
		no-op, which also makes the auto-load order irrelevant.
	-->
	<Binding name="DASEEKIBAGS2_TOGGLE" header="DASEEKIBAGS2" category="DASEEKIBAGS2">
		if DaseekiBags2_ToggleBags then DaseekiBags2_ToggleBags() end
	</Binding>
	<Binding name="DASEEKIBAGS2_BANK_TOGGLE" category="DASEEKIBAGS2">
		if DaseekiBags2_ToggleBank then DaseekiBags2_ToggleBank() end
	</Binding>
	<Binding name="DASEEKIBAGS2_FIND" category="DASEEKIBAGS2">
		if DaseekiBags2_ToggleFind then DaseekiBags2_ToggleFind() end
	</Binding>
</Bindings>
